doc: PredNamedCard: the card-name property NamedCard (gorge namePredicate NamedCard, CR 201.4): the candidate's name card is the reading source's chosen card name. The chosen name lives in the source permanent's chosen byte (the as-enters choice and a mid-resolution NameCard ask store it there, kernel repl_namecard.go), in a resolution's own answer for a source still on the stack (gorge Object.ChosenName), and in a host-bound emblem's frozen capture once a `DB$ Cleanup | ClearNamedCard$ True` wiped the source (gorge state.ContinuousEffect.ChosenName, Cheering Fanatic's ReduceCost ValidCard$ Card.NamedCard). A face-down candidate has no name (CR 708.2) and matches nothing. A reader with no chosen name to read fails closed, as gorge's empty ChosenName matches nothing. FilterFlags2 is full, so the word takes the one Pred slot (kernel filter_negations.go). 235: the free explicit ordinal below the 236+ family (PredRenowned took 236).
